  "notes": "Atmospheric Science option, University Park (of six options — Climate Science, Environmental Meteorology, General, Weather Forecasting and Communications, and Weather Risk Management are the others, each swapping in different 300/400-level METEO electives). Opens the College of Earth and Mineral Sciences. Reused the METEO catalog already scraped for Planetary Science and Astronomy. 'Professional Elective' and the 'METEO 436/437/454' and 'METEO 473/474' picks are modeled generically/as options, matching the bulletin's own flexible framing. Post-parens-fix re-scrape revealed CHEM 110's real prereq is MATH 22 (a placement threshold below Calc I that a MATH-140-track student has already tested past, but the bulletin's prereq text never says so explicitly), and MATH 22 has its own real chain (MATH 22 needs MATH 21, which needs MATH 4, which needs MATH 3) -- none of MATH 3/4/21/22 were in the plan, permanently blocking CHEM 110 (nothing else in this major's own sequence depends on CHEM 110, unlike ME/MATSCI, so no further cascade). Added MATH 3 (Semester 1), MATH 4 (Semester 2), MATH 21 (Semester 3), and MATH 22 (Semester 4) explicitly to complete the real chain, matching the fix used for MATSCI/ME's identical CHEM 110 gap. Raised max_credits_per_semester from 16 to 18 to absorb the extra 12cr (133cr total vs. 128cr capacity at the original 16cr/semester cap) without spilling into a 9th term.",
